{
  "_doc": "Language table shared by every checkup script. Regexes are Python syntax. 'risk' categories weight files in partition.py (events, async and state also mark stateful code); 'function' patterns find function headers ending at '{' on comment- and string-masked text; 'branch' approximates complexity; 'swallow' finds handlers that drop errors; 'imports' run on raw text, first non-empty group is the target; 'resolve' says how targets map to repo files. Only language constructs and standard libraries belong here. Folders whose names start with a dot are always skipped (tool and config folders). A project adds its own frameworks' markers with config 'risk_markers', names its frameworks call by themselves with 'framework_names', and extension mappings with 'extensions'.",
